{"language":"English","entry_date":"2026-11-16T09:33:31Z","relation":"Journal Name: Applied Catalysis B: Environment and Energy Journal Volume: 403","report_number":"BNL-230433-2026-JAAM","identifier":"SC0012704","country_publication":"United States","journal_type":"AM","doi":"10.1016/j.apcatb.2026.127584","description":"Direct ammonia protonic ceramic fuel cells (DA-PCFCs) represent a promising platform for efficient, low-emission power generation at intermediate temperatures; however, their performance is often constrained by sluggish anodic reaction kinetics. Herein, we demonstrate an active and durable DA-PCFC employing a self-assembled, heterostructured Ni-BaZr0.1Ce0.7Y0.1Yb0.1O3−δ (Ni-BZCYYb) cermet anode, decorated with in situ formed NiCo alloy and MoO3−δ catalyst under operating conditions. The resulting three-phase heterointerfaces synergistically enhance ammonia adsorption, activation, and decomposition kinetics. The cell delivers peak power densities of 0.464, 0.713, 1.051, and 1.566 W cm−2 at 550, 600, 650, and 700 °C, respectively, and exhibits stable operation for 100 h at 600 °C under a constant current density of 0.5 A cm−2. Density functional theory calculations identify the NiCo-MoO3−δ interface as the primary active site, providing favorable adsorption energetics and reduced reaction barriers. These findings establish an effective strategy for developing efficient electrocatalysts for high-performance, intermediate-temperature DA-PCFCs.","title":"In-situ self-assembled NiCo-MoO3-δ heterostructured catalysts for high-performance direct ammonia protonic ceramic fuel cells","other_number":"Journal ID: ISSN 0926-3373","contract_number":"SC0012704","publication_date":"2027-04-01T00:00:00Z","journal_volume":"403","osti_id":"17428540","journal_name":"Applied Catalysis B: Environment and Energy","product_type":"Journal Article","authors":["Chen, Liyan","Sasaki, Kotaro (ORCID:0000000324748323)","He, Fan","Yang, Xuan","Zhu, Feng","Hu, Feng","Sasaki, Kotaro